      "facts": [
        "The caller replaces every copy of the matched text, so a fuzzy match must be as unique as an exact one: an edit meant for one place must never rewrite its look-alikes elsewhere in the file.",
        "The matches tried after an exact one fails: extra leading indentation, then all whitespace ignored. `count` is how many places the loose form fits.",
        "Shorter lines (`}`, `});`, `</div>`) appear everywhere and say nothing about where the old string was meant to be.",
        "Curly quotes a model types as straight ones. `\\s` already covers non-breaking spaces.",
        "On a miss, the file's lines that best fit the old string, so the model can correct it in one retry instead of re-reading the file or guessing again. Lines compare by content, ignoring whitespace and curly quotes; the hint is shown only when at least half of the old string's lines fit.",
        "Indented to match: the replacement takes the same extra indentation."
      ],
