        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Code search failure messages now blame install only when ripgrep",
        "summary": "In `sdk/src/tools/code-search.ts`, the default `timeoutSeconds` for ripgrep is increased from 10 to 20 because shorter limits killed valid searches on large repositories. A new exported helper, `ripgrepFailureMessage`, replaces the inline error handling that previously appended installation advice to every ripgrep failure. The helper now includes that advice only when the error code is `ENOENT` and the expected binary path does not exist on the filesystem, preventing models from incorrectly assuming a missing installation when failures are caused by permissions or system load.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff introduces the `ripgrepFailureMessage` function in `sdk/src/tools/code-search.ts` and updates the default `timeoutSeconds` from 10 to 20. The new function checks `code === 'ENOENT' && !fs.existsSync(rgPath)` to conditionally append installation advice, replacing the previous unconditional error message that blamed the vendor binary for all spawn failures.",
