        "title": "CLI adds container, virtualization, and WSL fields to client",
        "summary": "The CLI's `x-freebuff-env` descriptor now includes three new fields: `ctr` for the container runtime, `vm` for the hypervisor or cloud provider, and `wsl` for Windows Subsystem for Linux detection. These fields are populated by a new `readMachineFacts` function that reads Linux-specific files like `/.dockerenv`, `/proc/1/cgroup`, and DMI sysfs entries, running in the background during the startup probe. The corresponding bucket types and constants were added to the shared client descriptor module to define the valid values for these new telemetry fields.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "New types `CONTAINER_BUCKETS` and `VIRTUALIZATION_BUCKETS` in `common/src/constants/freebuff-client-descriptor.ts`, and new functions `readMachineFacts`, `containerOf`, `virtualizationOf`, `isWsl` in `cli/src/utils/client-environment.ts` that read Linux DMI and cgroup files to append `ctr`, `vm`, and `wsl` fields to the `x-freebuff-env` descriptor.",
